cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MediGemma Field: Frontier healthcare for those beyond the frontier"
message: >-
  If you reference this project in research or articles, please cite using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: chyonek
    family-names: chyonek
abstract: >-
  An Android application that delivers WHO ETAT-aligned medical triage to
  remote and low-resource settings entirely on the user's phone, using
  Google's Gemma 4 model running on-device via LiteRT-LM. Designed for the
  4.5 billion people worldwide who lack access to basic health services
  (WHO 2024) and the 3.1 billion who fall in the GSMA "Usage Gap" (2025).

  Architecturally novel: a 3-layer "progressive enrichment" pipeline that
  routes work to the cheapest viable model layer first (ICD-11 keyword
  lookup → Gemma 4 Standard mode → Gemma 4 Thinking mode), saving battery,
  latency, and thermal budget on the entry-level phones that need them most.

  Privacy-by-design: no backend, no API key, no telemetry. Medical data
  never leaves the device. GDPR Article 17 (right to erasure) satisfied
  by app uninstall. Brand mark is religiously and culturally neutral
  (cupped hand offering a light, not a medical cross).
keywords:
  - on-device-ai
  - medical-triage
  - gemma-4
  - litert-lm
  - flutter
  - global-health
  - offline-first
  - multilingual
  - WHO-ETAT
  - ICD-11
  - hackathon
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/chyonek/medigemma_field"
url: "https://chyonek.github.io/medigemma_field/"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-18"

